{"case_id":"C021","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","attack_surface","input_semantics","state"],"commit_induced":"YES","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["decoder.do_decode_frame?","decoder.decode_dht?","decoder.calculate_huff_tables!","decoder.decode_sos?","decoder.decode_dri?","decoder.restart_frame!"],"reason":"S1 materially expands JPEG decoding behavior, but H0 exclusively builds and invokes the JSON decoder. H0 therefore cannot reach the newly added JPEG marker loop, DHT parsing and Huffman-table construction, SOS handling, or restart-related state transitions. Although the lack of JPEG coverage existed in S0, this commit materially aggravates it by adding substantial input-driven parsing and decoder state.","evidence":["H0 defines WUFFS_CONFIG__MODULE__JSON and invokes wuffs_json__decoder__decode_tokens and wuffs_aux::DecodeJson; it does not enable the JPEG module or instantiate decoder from std/jpeg/decode_jpeg.wuffs.","S1 adds an input-driven marker-processing loop to decoder.do_decode_frame?, including handling for DHT marker 0xC4, SOS marker 0xDA, DRI marker 0xDD, APPn markers, COM marker 0xFE, byte stuffing, and RSTn markers.","S1 adds decoder.decode_dht?, which reads attacker-controlled table identifiers, 16 code counts, and up to 256 symbols into huff_tables_symbols before invoking decoder.calculate_huff_tables!.","S1 adds decoder.calculate_huff_tables!, which derives dht_temp_bit_lengths, dht_temp_bit_strings, huff_tables_slow, and huff_tables_fast from parsed DHT data.","S1 changes decoder.decode_dri? to save saved_restart_interval before SOF and changes decoder.restart_frame! to restore restart_interval and clear all eight seen_dht entries.","In S0, decoder.do_decode_frame? proceeded to the placeholder gradient generation without the new post-SOF marker and Huffman-table parsing, so the uncovered JPEG attack surface is materially larger in S1."],"recommended_action":"Add or extend a project-owned JPEG fuzz harness that initializes the JPEG decoder and drives the image-decoder call sequence through decode_image_config?, decode_frame_config?, decode_frame?, and restart_frame!, with fuzz-controlled JPEG marker streams covering DHT, SOS, DRI, RSTn, APPn, COM, malformed payload lengths, and repeated decode/restart state transitions."}
